tle-named-pancake-makes-a-triumphant-return-to-the-ocean-after-months-of-rehabilitation-180989205/</link><description>这只被冻晕的海龟去年秋天在科德角获救，现已完全康复。这只爬行动物的性别尚不清楚，估计年龄在 2 至 5 岁之间，释放时重 11 磅</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-endangered-kemps-ridley-sea-turtle-named-pancake-makes-a-triumphant-return-to-the-ocean-after-months-of-rehabilitation-180989205/</guid></item><item><title>双语者的大脑如何处理两种语言？新研究表明两者都依赖相同的神经线路</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-does-a-bilingual-speakers-brain-process-two-languages-new-research-suggests-that-both-rely-on-the-same-neural-wiring-180989202/</link><description>科学家们长期以来一直想知道双语使用者大脑中是否有不同的神经机制控制着每种语言。最近一项针对同时讲英语和西班牙语的人的研究暗示存在单一“语法引擎”</description><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 20:29:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-does-a-bilingual-speakers-brain-process-two-languages-new-research-suggests-that-both-rely-on-the-same-neural-wiring-180989202/</guid></item><item><title>法国海关在试图越境后扣押了这幅马克·夏加尔的蚀刻画长达二十年。现在即将公开展示</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/french-customs-detained-this-marc-chagall-etching-for-two-decades-after-an-attempted-border-crossing-now-its-headed-for-public-display-180989204/</link><description>在荒诞的场景中，一名杂技演员坐在小提琴上，该场景借鉴了俄罗斯艺术家最喜欢的主题</description><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 19:08:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/french-customs-detained-this-marc-chagall-etching-for-two-decades-after-an-attempted-border-crossing-now-its-headed-for-public-display-180989204/</guid></item><item><title>艺术侦探发现了这位苏格兰先驱画家遗失的“极其重要”的印度精英女性肖像</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/art-sleuths-discovered-a-long-lost-and-enormously-important-portrait-of-an-elite-indian-woman-by-this-pioneering-scottish-painter-180989201/</link><description>凯瑟琳·里德 (Katherine Read) 在移居印度之前是伦敦最时尚的肖像创作者之一。她在描绘妇女和儿童方面取得了成功</description><pubD